// XFAIL: RT-446g: (RT-446's mechanism, a fn's result) `fn mk(x: &u64) -> R { x }` with `type R = &'static u64` is accepted: the result's written 'static is not seen, so it is read as elided (borrowing x); rustc refuses mk ("lifetime may not live long enough") (0.30.2)
// From the g302static work (its pre/pre03; RT-446's root, the region
// walk not following an alias). Since v0.30.1 at least. On this build
// no use after free follows from it: a caller that drops the argument
// while the result lives, `let r = mk(&*b); drop(b);`, is refused at
// the drop (borrowck.move_borrowed), since the result is taken to borrow
// x. RT-C301-19 is the same root's false-positive side.
// ERROR: line 12
type R = &'static u64;

fn mk(x: &u64) -> R {
    x
}

fn main() {
    let k = 7u64;
    println("{}", mk(&k));
}
